  "findings": [
    "Serial presented runs spend about 15-16 ms per frame in waitUntilCompleted, while encoding plus commit costs about 0.05-0.06 ms. nextDrawable averages about 0.03 ms in those serial runs.",
    "A/B/B/A serial versus three-inflight presented trials finish at 59.83,108.66,105.04,59.29 completed commands/s. This improves the authored harness only; it is not a driver or all-game speedup.",
    "With three in-flight frames on both sides, private offscreen reaches 1306.58-1414.73, shared offscreen 479.05-565.49 and presented drawable 107.38-120.65 completed commands/s. A substantial gap remains after matching in-flight bounds.",
    "No-present drawable trials reach 117.24-120.85 commands/s with about 7.05-8.22 ms in nextDrawable. A later interleaved no-present trial reaches 114.26, with 8.20 ms in nextDrawable. Omitting final presentation does not remove the ceiling.",
    "Drawable reports Managed storage (1), usage 23. Persistent Managed offscreen reports storage 1, usage 4 and reaches 1349.46-1461.77 commands/s. Storage mode alone does not explain the gap; usage, IOSurface backing and lifecycle differ.",
    "The supported next investigation is drawable/IOSurface recycling and synchronization, including resource paging and compositor interaction. These tests do not isolate the exact underlying wait or prove that a single host blit is responsible."
  ],
  "hostObservations": {
    "scope": "Separate short serial-mode trials; GPU-wide counters include other Windows and guest workloads. Approximate middle samples, not exclusive per-process attribution.",
    "presentedPcieMeanMBps": {
      "rx": 14494,
      "tx": 7021
    },
    "noPresentPcieMeanMBps": {
      "rx": 37.7,
      "tx": 3814
    },
    "interpretation": "Large transfer traffic accompanies presentation; no causal byte attribution or bandwidth-only bottleneck is established. Private offscreen samples were transient/mixed and are excluded from that comparison.",
    "presentMode": "MAILBOX",
    "presentFences": false,
    "queueWaitIdleDuringCapturedSteadyTrials": 0,
    "queueWaitIdleSourceCallsites": "Retired swapchain bound and window end, not every frame. The startup no-present-fences warning does not establish a steady-state queue-idle bottleneck."
  },
  "checks": {
    "acceptedRuns": 24,
    "allExitZero": true,
    "allFirstFrameWitnessesPass": true,
    "allGpuCommandErrors": 0,
    "newHostGpuFatalExecFaultHangOrKernelPanicObserved": false,
    "latestSourceGuestCompileWarningsAsErrors": "passed",
    "runtimeDllRestoredBeforeAcceptedTrials": true,
    "imageMemoryCacheCandidate": "parked, not active and not qualified by this investigation",
    "postTrialComputeVerifiedValues": 4096,
    "guest_presents": 43713,
    "host_presents": 43707,
    "log_level": 3,
    "display_width": 3840,
    "display_height": 2160
  },
  "limits": [
    "Short repeated diagnostics with concurrent desktop activity; no process-isolated PCIe attribution or physical display-frame timestamps.",
    "4K render target in a 960x540-point window; not a fullscreen 4K game benchmark.",
    "Three slots bound in-flight work but persistent offscreen targets and a drawable pool have different resource lifecycles.",
    "Managed offscreen versus drawable also differs in texture usage and IOSurface backing; Managed alone is ruled out, individual remaining costs are not isolated.",
    "framebufferOnly=false permits the first-frame readback. Apps using framebufferOnly=true need a separate comparison.",
    "Guest-reported GPU time includes bridge scheduling/completion-detection costs; it is not an isolated hardware shader duration. Pipeline mode does not sample it.",
    "CoreGraphics returned 0 for refresh; AppKit returned 58 maximum fps. Configured 60 Hz is not a measured physical display cadence.",
    "Earlier 15-36 versus 146-270 observations used different runtime/background conditions and serial waiting; they are superseded by the controlled mode comparisons here.",
    "Two rejected development harness runs had pending-status validation/semaphore-disposal bugs, corrected before accepted pipeline trials. They are not GPU-driver failures.",
    "No broader Metal compatibility, new Geekbench score, all-game performance improvement or steady 4K160 claim."
  ],
